---
/** The pieces of a PeerShare session, and the path of one request. */
---

<figure>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 780 380" role="img" aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc">
    <title id="arch-title">PeerShare's architecture</title>
    <desc id="arch-desc">
      The Guest's browser holds the service page in an isolated origin and the PeerShare page.
      Both browsers connect through the relay, encrypted end to end with Noise, or directly over
      WebRTC, encrypted with DTLS whose keys were exchanged over the Noise channel. The Sharer's PeerShare tab is the hub; it reaches local services through the local
      proxy and remote https services directly.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="#1f6f5c"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <style>
      .box { fill: #fff; stroke: #d4d4cf; stroke-width: 1.2; }
      .zone { fill: none; stroke: #b9b9b3; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
      .t { font: 600 13px system-ui, sans-serif; fill: #18181b; }
      .s { font: 12px system-ui, sans-serif; fill: #5f5f66; }
      .m { font: 11px ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; fill: #5f5f66; }
      .z { font: 600 11px system-ui, sans-serif; fill: #8a8a85; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
      .flow { stroke: #1f6f5c; stroke-width: 2; fill: none; marker-end: url(#arrow); }
      .enc { stroke: #1f6f5c; stroke-width: 2.5; fill: none; stroke-dasharray: 7 5; }
      .relay { stroke: #b9b9b3; stroke-width: 1.5; fill: none; }
      .lock { fill: #e7f2ee; stroke: #1f6f5c; }
    </style>

    <!-- Guest's browser -->
    <rect class="zone" x="12" y="28" width="236" height="300" rx="14"></rect>
    <text class="z" x="26" y="50">GUEST'S BROWSER</text>
    <rect class="box" x="30" y="66" width="200" height="86" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="t" x="44" y="90">The service, isolated</text>
    <text class="m" x="44" y="110">x7…k2.s.httpeers.net</text>
    <text class="s" x="44" y="130">own origin, storage and</text>
    <text class="s" x="44" y="145">ServiceWorker</text>
    <rect class="box" x="30" y="214" width="200" height="94" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="t" x="44" y="238">PeerShare page</text>
    <text class="m" x="44" y="258">peershare.httpeers.net</text>
    <text class="s" x="44" y="278">the Guest's key and</text>
    <text class="s" x="44" y="293">membership token</text>
    <path class="flow" d="M130 152 V212"></path>
    <text class="s" x="138" y="186">MessagePort</text>

    <!-- Relay -->
    <rect class="box" x="300" y="40" width="180" height="70" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="t" x="314" y="64">Relay</text>
    <text class="m" x="314" y="84">relay.httpeers.net</text>
    <text class="s" x="314" y="100">forwards ciphertext only</text>
    <path class="relay" d="M230 240 C 270 180, 300 140, 330 110"></path>
    <path class="relay" d="M550 240 C 510 180, 480 140, 450 110"></path>

    <!-- The encrypted channel -->
    <path class="enc" d="M232 262 H548"></path>
    <rect class="lock" x="304" y="244" width="172" height="36" rx="8"></rect>
    <text class="t" x="318" y="262">Encrypted end to end</text>
    <text class="s" x="318" y="276">Noise · DTLS if direct</text>

    <!-- Sharer's browser -->
    <rect class="zone" x="532" y="28" width="236" height="300" rx="14"></rect>
    <text class="z" x="546" y="50">SHARER'S COMPUTER</text>
    <rect class="box" x="550" y="214" width="200" height="94" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="t" x="564" y="238">PeerShare tab = hub</text>
    <text class="s" x="564" y="258">Sharer's key, members,</text>
    <text class="s" x="564" y="273">the services</text>
    <text class="s" x="564" y="293">checks every request</text>
    <rect class="box" x="550" y="66" width="96" height="86" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="t" x="560" y="90">Local proxy</text>
    <text class="m" x="560" y="110">127.0.0.1</text>
    <text class="s" x="560" y="130">→ localhost,</text>
    <text class="s" x="560" y="145">LAN</text>
    <rect class="box" x="654" y="66" width="96" height="86" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="t" x="664" y="90">Your app</text>
    <text class="m" x="664" y="110">:5173</text>
    <path class="flow" d="M598 212 V154"></path>
    <path class="flow" d="M646 109 H652"></path>

    <!-- Direct -->
    <rect class="box" x="550" y="344" width="200" height="30" rx="8"></rect>
    <text class="s" x="562" y="364">or a remote https site, read directly</text>
    <path class="flow" d="M650 308 V342"></path>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    One request: the service page in the Guest's isolated origin asks for <code>/app.js</code>;
    its ServiceWorker hands it to the Guest's PeerShare page, which sends it over the encrypted
    channel to the Sharer's tab; the tab checks the Guest, fetches the file through the local
    proxy (or directly), and the answer travels back the same way.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
